# Architecture Boundaries

- Direction: `app -> modules -> components/lib/api`.
- `src/app` routes stay thin and delegate to `src/modules/<scope>/pages/*`.
- `src/components` and `src/lib` are shared layers and must not import from `src/modules`.
- `src/api` is generated and can be consumed by modules/shared, never edited manually.

## Required patterns

- Keep domain logic in module scopes (`src/modules/auth`, `src/modules/brands`, etc.).
- Inside a module scope, colocate page-specific logic under `pages/*`.
- Cross-module imports should use stable module surfaces when available.

## Prohibited patterns

- Circular imports across `app`, `modules`, `components`, and `lib`.
- Importing `src/modules/*` from shared UI primitives.
- Introducing `route-entry` indirection for module pages.
